All right. And Sean? I'm going to go a little bit more into detail here.

00:30:28.840 --> 00:30:35.900
Most games, most arcade games where you're doing some really, like, obtuse thing to make

00:30:35.900 --> 00:30:41.360
it a game at least has some really bullshit story reason for why you're doing it.

00:30:41.380 --> 00:30:46.140
And in this game, like, you get the whole, like, who this person is, like Clarice.

00:30:46.260 --> 00:30:49.660
She has blue hair. You're on the run from the police, sure.

00:30:49.840 --> 00:30:54.140
But there's never an explanation as to why you're coding highways in paint.

00:30:54.380 --> 00:30:58.840
I don't understand the core conceit or why I'm doing it.

00:30:58.920 --> 00:31:02.620
And for that reason alone, it is unessential.

00:31:03.900 --> 00:31:06.520
I feel like I wish you didn't say that.

00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:14.020
Because I think that the reason why she paints the roads is because she's such a world traveler

00:31:14.020 --> 00:31:20.500
and an aficionado of these cities that she has to see everything there is to see in these cities.

00:31:20.680 --> 00:31:23.440
And she must, you know, like, go touch every part.

00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:24.680
She's painting the town white.

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:26.960
Right. Exactly. And so...

00:31:26.960 --> 00:31:28.320
It's a city, not a town. If she was just...

00:31:28.320 --> 00:31:30.200
But, yeah. But if she was just collecting things, right?

00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:35.380
She'd be another, like, Instagram, you know, simple person who's just there for the picture

00:31:35.380 --> 00:31:37.100
with the Statue of Liberty and stuff like that.

00:31:37.100 --> 00:31:38.180
So she's Banksy. Yeah.

00:31:38.320 --> 00:31:39.200
She is, like...

00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:41.340
Yeah. She's a... And that's why the cops are after her.

00:31:42.240 --> 00:31:45.020
She's vandalizing the city with her propaganda.

00:31:46.020 --> 00:31:47.560
It's just... Which is white paint.

00:31:47.560 --> 00:31:49.080
I thought this was all really clear.

00:31:49.200 --> 00:31:50.540
There's no propaganda.

00:31:50.820 --> 00:31:51.640
It's white paint.

00:31:52.400 --> 00:31:57.680
Yeah. It's funny how the back of the box just kind of says, like, you're...

00:31:57.680 --> 00:32:00.540
Race your speed demon car from New York to Tokyo in record time.

00:32:01.060 --> 00:32:03.860
And then with the cops and the enemy on your tail.

00:32:04.040 --> 00:32:06.420
But, like, why? Because you're going too fast?

00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:08.080
Like, stop being a...

00:32:08.080 --> 00:32:09.340
Like, you're going to get somebody hurt.

00:32:09.580 --> 00:32:13.640
Like, slow down. We also didn't mention, though, the manual does say that you've broken into an exclusive

00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:15.220
paint store in New York City.

00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:17.620
Yes. But I still don't know why I'm using it.

00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:18.620
Why you need to use it.

00:32:18.780 --> 00:32:20.800
But that is why you're on the run, at least.

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:24.020
You know that. I don't know why we need to cover every inch of the road with paint.

00:32:24.440 --> 00:32:30.600
Do you think that countries would, like, continue to try to track down someone who stole paint

00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:32.300
from a local store in New York City?

00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:33.720
Well, if it's exclusive. Yeah.

00:32:34.200 --> 00:32:36.220
It's not... This isn't, like, Sherwin-Williams.

00:32:36.320 --> 00:32:37.220
This is a...

00:32:37.920 --> 00:32:39.480
This is an exclusive store.

00:32:39.540 --> 00:32:40.460
Very good. Yeah. That's true.

00:32:40.600 --> 00:32:41.880
This is... Yeah. All right.

00:32:42.320 --> 00:32:44.960
As for me, this game is not essential.

